window.docContents[151].resolve({"/Solver/#solver":{"contents":"Similar to terms, solvers come in typed and untyped flavors, though they do not differ by much. The main differences are\n\n* typed Solver.assert requires a Term Bool, instead of a Term for the untyped version, and* typed model/value-retrieval as we will see below.\n\nThe rest of this section discusses typed solvers.\n\nSolvers are tied to cvc5's notion of term manager, which means they are manager-scoped with a Cvc.Ω instance just like sorts and terms.\n\n\n\nopen Cvc Typed\nvariable [Ω]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level API for CVC5","header":"6. Solver","id":"/Solver/#solver"}});